Once you see him, nothing can save you.

2
00:07:35,172 --> 00:07:41,172
Sinister is a horror, thriller, mystery film directed by Scott Derrickson.

3
00:11:22,758 --> 00:11:28,758
True-crime writer Ellison Oswalt is in a slump; he hasn't had a best seller in
more than 10 years and is becoming increasingly desperate for a hit.

4
00:15:10,344 --> 00:15:16,344
So, when he discovers the existence of a snuff film showing the
deaths of a family, he vows to solve the mystery.

5
00:18:57,931 --> 00:19:03,931
He moves his own family into the victims' home and gets to work.

6
00:22:45,517 --> 00:22:51,517
However, when old film footage and other clues hint at the presence of a
supernatural force, Ellison learns that living in the house may be fatal.

7
00:26:33,103 --> 00:26:39,103
Ellison Oswalt, played by Ethan Hawke.

8
00:30:20,689 --> 00:30:26,689
Tracy Oswalt, played by Juliet Rylance.

9
00:34:08,275 --> 00:34:14,275
Professor Jonas, played by Vincent D'Onofrio.

10
00:37:55,862 --> 00:38:01,862
Deputy, played by James Ransone.

11
00:41:43,448 --> 00:41:49,448
Sheriff, played by Fred Thompson.

12
00:45:31,034 --> 00:45:37,034
Ashley Oswalt, played by Clare Foley.

13
00:49:18,620 --> 00:49:24,620
Sinister is a 2012 supernatural horror film directed by
Scott Derrickson, who co-wrote with C.

14
00:53:06,206 --> 00:53:12,206
Robert Cargill.

15
00:56:53,793 --> 00:56:59,793
It stars Ethan Hawke as a struggling true-crime writer whose discovery of snuff films depicting gruesome
murders and strange supernatural elements in his new house puts his family in danger.

16
01:00:41,379 --> 01:00:47,379
Juliet Rylance, Fred Thompson, James Ransone, Clare Foley, and
Michael Hall D'Addario are featured in supporting roles.

17
01:04:28,965 --> 01:04:34,965
Sinister was inspired by a nightmare Cargill had
after watching the 2002 film The Ring.

18
01:08:16,551 --> 01:08:22,551
Principal photography on Sinister began in Autumn of 2011 on Long
Island, New York with a production budget of $3 million.

19
01:12:04,137 --> 01:12:10,137
To add to the authenticity of old home movies and snuff films, the Super 8
segments were shot on actual Super 8 cameras and film stock.

20
01:15:51,724 --> 01:15:57,724
It premiered at the SXSW festival on March 10, 2012.

21
01:19:39,310 --> 01:19:45,310
It was released in the United Kingdom on October 5, 2012,
and in the United States on October 12.

22
01:23:26,896 --> 01:23:32,896
Critics praised its acting, direction, cinematography, and atmosphere, but
criticised its use of jump scares and other horror clichés.

23
01:27:14,482 --> 01:27:20,482
It was a box office success, grossing $87.7 million
against its budget of $3 million.

24
01:31:02,068 --> 01:31:08,068
The resulting financial success led to a sequel, released in 2015.

25
01:34:49,655 --> 01:34:55,655
It has since developed a reputation for scariness
and is considered a cult classic.

26
01:38:37,241 --> 01:38:43,241
A 2020 study by Broadband Choices named Sinister the scariest film
ever made, based on an analysis of viewer heart rates.

27
01:42:24,827 --> 01:42:30,827
The film explores themes of drowning, pennsylvania,
usa, writing, child murder, snuff.

28
01:46:12,413 --> 01:46:18,413
The tone is dark and mind_bending and emotional.
